{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"New user passwords must be at least 12 literal characters long.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active PAM password stack sets pam_cracklib minlen=12 and disables all character-class credits, preventing shorter passwords from satisfying the length calculation. The same policy remained active after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f11b0443de2845da","cmd-9c608449819042f5","cmd-42a8d54c16fc4354","cmd-5630d086455f4afd","cmd-fc17c2e0af084fc2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"New user passwords must contain at least three different character classes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active pam_cracklib rule sets minclass=3. Installed documentation defines this as requiring three of the four supported classes. The configuration persisted across restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f11b0443de2845da","cmd-9c608449819042f5","cmd-42a8d54c16fc4354","cmd-5630d086455f4afd","cmd-fc17c2e0af084fc2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were identical before and after execution. The implementation uses the already-installed CentOS 5 PAM/cracklib packages, including pam-0.99.6.2-12.el5, with no evidence of package installation or platform replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3b9601f2bf34cdc","cmd-2c9b0dafd641435f","cmd-5630d086455f4afd","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.82,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.52,"summary":"Final state was clean and healthy: temporary users, processes, backup files, and test artifacts were removed; /tmp returned to its baseline inventory; SSH recovered; and lifecycle data shows only the required boot-identity change. However, the executor performed many state-changing troubleshooting experiments that did not contribute reliable final behavioral evidence. Reverted local-account/password experiments occurred in cmd-d082606dcc1b48d4, cmd-294bb7dedff44d18, cmd-1ecf405269ec40a3, cmd-17e7785c0b594d60, cmd-2320b9ab24cc4829, cmd-eab2804d158c490b, cmd-2f59c52348254af6, cmd-3d9f3151aca34169, and cmd-493ef77371684385. Reverted script/TTY probe files were created by cmd-819ef6a6620042e9 and cmd-9f35f4fdb97648f9. Reverted SSH-based experiments created temporary accounts, homes, secrets, keys, or authorized_keys in cmd-354752e53792473a, cmd-8fe0feabc5dd4319, cmd-5f7e2cd2709e4178, cmd-296455381c4942bb, cmd-06e97ed701004292, cmd-e258d3a408854f02, cmd-724974dbe9c14387, and cmd-d0c6f23a11b84b23. One experiment also left a hung process requiring explicit cleanup. These mutations were bounded and ultimately restored, but their number and repeated account/shadow manipulation materially reduce hygiene.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d082606dcc1b48d4","cmd-294bb7dedff44d18","cmd-1ecf405269ec40a3","cmd-17e7785c0b594d60","cmd-2320b9ab24cc4829","cmd-819ef6a6620042e9","cmd-eab2804d158c490b","cmd-2f59c52348254af6","cmd-3d9f3151aca34169","cmd-493ef77371684385","cmd-9f35f4fdb97648f9","cmd-354752e53792473a","cmd-8fe0feabc5dd4319","cmd-5f7e2cd2709e4178","cmd-296455381c4942bb","cmd-06e97ed701004292","cmd-e258d3a408854f02","cmd-724974dbe9c14387","cmd-d0c6f23a11b84b23","cmd-7d577d1ceee44f30","cmd-42a8d54c16fc4354","cmd-fc17c2e0af084fc2","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct final configuration and platform observations. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged restart, observed downtime, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered PAM policy, SSH service, and account data. Confidence is below maximum because behavioral password-change testing was inconclusive. Operational hygiene is only moderate because numerous unsuccessful, state-changing validation experiments were performed, although their artifacts were ultimately removed.","limitations":["No representative non-root password-change test successfully demonstrated both rejection of invalid candidates and acceptance of a compliant candidate. Several harness attempts failed before completing interaction; a root-driven passwd --stdin test accepted a weak value and is not representative of an ordinary user's PAM-enforced change.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation and the failed-services probe could not inspect this non-systemd platform. Their outputs were unchanged before and after, but they do not independently establish comprehensive package or service health.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory PAM configuration, so final policy assessment relies on the captured executor commands that directly read the active PAM rule.","Restart evidence is otherwise strong and independently cross-checked: boot identity changed from 0aff472a-3abe-4d51-8000-000000000000 to 0bcd700a-5efd-443b-8000-000000000000 in both executor and fixed lifecycle observations."]}
